# The conformance kit is the point of the package, not a development detail:
# it is what lets somebody who was not here re-run the checks against their own
# implementation. setuptools picks up tests/*.py on its own and leaves the
# vectors behind, so an unpacked sdist carried the test that reads them and not
# the files it reads. Named explicitly here so that stays fixed.
include LICENSE
include README.md
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include tests/conformance *.json
recursive-include tests/conformance *.xml
